{
  "title": "The if / else Statement — Two Paths",
  "subtitle": "Handling True and False Paths with else and elif",
  "topic": "4.2 • TWO PATHS",
  "body": "<div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 18px; width: 100%;\">\n  <div style=\"text-align: center; margin-bottom: 4px; width: 100%;\">\n    <div style=\"display: inline-block; background-color: #ffffff; border: 3px solid #111111; box-shadow: 4px 4px 0px #111111; padding: 4px 14px; margin-bottom: 10px; font-weight: 900; font-size: 12px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1px;\">\n      4.2 • Branching Logic\n    </div>\n    <h1 style=\"font-family: 'Title', 'Body', sans-serif; font-size: 30px; font-weight: 900; color: #111111; margin: 0 0 8px 0; text-transform: uppercase;\">\n      The <hlt>if / else</hlt> Branch\n    </h1>\n    <p style=\"font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600; color: #222222; margin: 0 auto; max-width: 640px;\">\n      When an <code>if</code> condition is False, the <code>else</code> block provides an automatic fallback branch so your program always responds!\n    </p>\n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 16px;\">\n    <div style=\"background: #86efac; border: 3px solid #111111; box-shadow: 5px 5px 0px #111111; border-radius: 4px; padding: 18px;\">\n      <span style=\"display: inline-block; background-color: #ffffff; color: #111111; border: 2px solid #111111; box-shadow: 2px 2px 0px #111111; padding: 2px 8px; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 900; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 8px;\">\n        Path A (True)\n      </span>\n      <h3 style=\"font-family: 'Title', 'Body', sans-serif; font-size: 18px; font-weight: 900; color: #111111; margin: 0 0 8px 0;\">The if Block</h3>\n      <p style=\"font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; color: #111111; margin-bottom: 10px;\">Executes only when condition evaluates to True.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <div style=\"background: #fca5a5; border: 3px solid #111111; box-shadow: 5px 5px 0px #111111; border-radius: 4px; padding: 18px;\">\n      <span style=\"display: inline-block; background-color: #ffffff; color: #111111; border: 2px solid #111111; box-shadow: 2px 2px 0px #111111; padding: 2px 8px; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 900; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 8px;\">\n        Path B (False)\n      </span>\n      <h3 style=\"font-family: 'Title', 'Body', sans-serif; font-size: 18px; font-weight: 900; color: #111111; margin: 0 0 8px 0;\">The else Block</h3>\n      <p style=\"font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; color: #111111; margin-bottom: 10px;\">Executes automatically when the if condition is False.</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"background: #0d1117; border: 2px solid #111111; box-shadow: 4px 4px 0 #111111; padding: 14px; font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; color: #f0f6fc; font-size: 14px; border-radius: 4px;\">\n    balance = <span style=\"color: #7ee787;\">20</span><br/>\n    item_cost = <span style=\"color: #7ee787;\">50</span><br/><br/>\n    <span style=\"color: #ff7b72;\">if</span> balance &gt;= item_cost:<br/>\n    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span style=\"color: #79c0ff;\">print</span>(<span style=\"color: #a5d6ff;\">\"Purchase Successful\"</span>)<br/>\n    <span style=\"color: #ff7b72;\">else</span>:<br/>\n    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span style=\"color: #79c0ff;\">print</span>(<span style=\"color: #a5d6ff;\">\"Insufficient Funds\"</span>)  <span style=\"color: #8b949e;\"># Outputs: Insufficient Funds</span>\n  </div>\n</div>"
}